.TH "ELEMENT.MOUSEOVER_EVENT" "3JS" "July 28, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
Element.mouseover_event \- Element: mouseover event
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]mouseover\f[B]\f[R] event is fired at an
\f[CR]Element\f[R] when a pointing device (such as a mouse or trackpad)
is used to move the cursor onto the element or one of its child
elements.
.PP
If the target element has child elements, \f[CR]mouseout\f[R] and
\f[CR]mouseover\f[R] events fire as the mouse moves over the boundaries
of these elements too, not just the target element itself.
Usually, \f[CR]mouseenter\f[R] and \f[CR]mouseleave\f[R] events\(cq
behavior is more sensible, because they are not affected by moving into
child elements.
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in methods like \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R], or set
an event handler property.
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqmouseover\(dq, (event) => { })

onmouseover = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
A \f[CR]MouseEvent\f[R].
Inherits from \f[CR]UIEvent\f[R] and \f[CR]Event\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
The following example illustrates the difference between
\f[CR]mouseover\f[R] and \f[CR]mouseenter\f[R] events.
.SS HTML
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]ul\f[R] id=\(dqtest\(dq>
  <\f[B]li\f[R]>item 1</\f[B]li\f[R]>
  <\f[B]li\f[R]>item 2</\f[B]li\f[R]>
  <\f[B]li\f[R]>item 3</\f[B]li\f[R]>
</\f[B]ul\f[R]>
.EE
.SS JavaScript
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] test = document.getElementById(\(dqtest\(dq);

\f[I]// This handler will be executed only once when the cursor\f[R]
\f[I]// moves over the unordered list\f[R]
test.addEventListener(\(dqmouseenter\(dq, (event) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  \f[I]// highlight the mouseenter target\f[R]
  event.target.style.color = \(dqpurple\(dq;

  \f[I]// reset the color after a short delay\f[R]
  setTimeout(() \f[B]=>\f[R] {
    event.target.style.color = \(dq\(dq;
  }, 500);
});

\f[I]// This handler will be executed every time the cursor\f[R]
\f[I]// is moved over a different list item\f[R]
test.addEventListener(\(dqmouseover\(dq, (event) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  \f[I]// highlight the mouseover target\f[R]
  event.target.style.color = \(dqorange\(dq;

  \f[I]// reset the color after a short delay\f[R]
  setTimeout(() \f[B]=>\f[R] {
    event.target.style.color = \(dq\(dq;
  }, 500);
});
.EE
